{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typedactor", "label": "TypedActor<T>", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The runtime host that interprets a Behavior value; internally an Actor<T> subclass with the same mailbox, dispatcher and supervisor tree, whose onReceive delegates into the currently active Behavior."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_onreceive", "label": "TypedActor.onReceive", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_prestart", "label": "TypedActor.preStart (initial resolution)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_resolution_loop", "label": "Behavior resolution loop", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Composed behaviors unwrap one layer at a time until a leaf receive or sentinel is reached; each wrapper has its side effect once and disappears, so the final shape is a plain receive value while the framework keeps the strategy and timer scheduler."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_scope_stack", "label": "Supervise scopes are a stack, not a slot", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A walk past two supervise wrappers records two scopes, innermost last; failures are offered innermost-first and Escalate moves one scope out, so an outer wrapper is never silently displaced by an inner one. A restart shortens the stack only below the deciding scope."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_wrapper_cycle_bound", "label": "64-hop wrapper cycle bound", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A setup that returns itself or a recursing supervise is bounded at 64 hops; the resolver then throws so the misconfiguration surfaces loudly instead of spinning forever."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_transitions", "label": "Behavior transitions (four outcomes)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_lifecycle_signals", "label": "Lifecycle signals: post-stop / pre-restart / terminated", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Invoked from the framework postStop / preRestart / Terminated-delivery hooks; the return value works like the receive handler."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_initial_behavior_gotchas", "label": "Initial-behavior gotchas", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Behaviors.same as initial is meaningless and is treated as empty (the actor exists but drops everything, usually surfacing a logic bug); Behaviors.stopped as initial stops the actor in preStart, useful when an external check at spawn time decides whether the actor should exist."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typed_untyped_seam", "label": "Typed/untyped seam", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Failures inside a typed handler reach the typed supervisor first and only carry on to the parent once the wrapper is out of restarts; child spawning is cast-free because the runtime wraps each child in another TypedActor."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_watch", "label": "Cross-form watching is one-way", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A typed actor may watch an untyped ref or vice versa; termination arrives as a terminated signal on the typed side and as a Terminated message on the untyped side."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_spawntyped", "label": "system.spawnTyped / context.spawnTyped", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The spawn helpers close over the Behavior value and produce a fresh TypedActor each time the actor factory runs, which is why constructing TypedActor by hand does not behave like a fresh actor across restarts."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typedactor_helper", "label": "typedActor helper", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typedactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_onreceive", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typedactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_prestart", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typedactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_resolution_loop", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typedactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_transitions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typedactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_lifecycle_signals", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typedactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_initial_behavior_gotchas", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/typed-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typedactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_typed_actor_typed_untyped_seam", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "sourc